The use of `compareAndSet` on the `AtomicBoolean initialized` allows multiple threads to enter the `matches` method concurrently. If one thread calls `matches` and sets `initialized` to `true`, another thread could still enter the method before the first thread has completed the `initialized(context)` call, leading to unexpected errors due to incomplete initialization.

